Generate the autocompletion script for powershell.

To load completions in your current shell session:

        cron-person completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

To load completions for every new session, add the output of the above command
to your powershell profile.

Usage:
  cron-person completion powershell [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help              help for powershell
      --no-descriptions   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
      --config string   Path to custom configuration file (default:
                        $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string    Path to custom authorization state file (default:
                        $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
